# Review Ledger: assembly-catalog-contract Change Set {#el:review-ledger}

This review ledger covers the `assembly-catalog-contract` change-set within the `striatum-next/passes/work-graph-assembly-c` work graph. The review validates the internal coherence of the catalog additions, the correctness of the driver implementation for the new `subject-assembly` pass, and the consistency of the artifact declarations with the accepted design predicates (work-graph-integrated@2).

## Summary

The change-set introduces the `subject-assembly` pass as a declared, independent, deterministic second producer of the `Change Set` (L5) artifact, alongside the existing `build` pass. The implementation correctly registers the pass in the catalog, updates the driver's `LoadCatalog` and `ProducerOf` logic to handle multiple producers without nondeterminism, and provides comprehensive tests verifying the registration, lifecycle constraints, and producer consistency. The changes are internally coherent, fully adhere to the RFC 0010 work-graph-integrated@2 predicate, and do not introduce any predicate-blocking defects. The pass is correctly gated, consumes the required inputs at the accepted lifecycle, and produces a deterministic result over the anchored base.

## Findings

